Error [E-WEB-ABI-TYPE]: `Point` cannot cross the JS/WASM boundary on a `#WasmExport` parameter
  --> tests/ui/web_abi_type.jet:7:4
    |
  7 | fn export_bad(p: Point) Int -> p.x
    |    ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Web exports and imports only admit ABI-safe types (scalars, `String`, `List`/`Map` of ABI-safe values, and `#[Codable]` structs/enums)
 Fix: Use a scalar, `String`, a `List`/`Map` of ABI-safe values, or a `#[Codable]` struct/enum whose fields are ABI-safe
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-WEB-ABI-TYPE
